:: StoryTitle
The Meridian Key

:: StoryData
{
  "ifid": "<generated by Twine>",
  "format": "Inkjot",
  "format-version": "0.6.0",
  "start": "hangar"
}

:: Inklink [config]
(((
Ex 11: a JRPG-style `game`, solo, one level and its boss. Four scouts of
the Lantern, the rebellion's eyes, have come into an Auric Dominion relay
under a glacier to steal the Meridian Key, the chart that tells the
Dominion's fleets where to jump. Getting in is the easy part.

One of the four leads: you look through them, and you give the other three
one command each, every round. The lead can change hands between fights.

A draft for milestone 23, written before the words it needs exist. New
words it asks for (see `examples/drafts/README.md`):

| Word | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `encounter orrel, sentry_a, sentry_b` | Several opponents in one encounter; each takes its move every round, in the order named |
| `~ as fight` | The kind of exchange (decided: `fight`, `negotiation`, `seduction`, `discovery`, `other`) |
| `~ by quill` | On a Link: the act is that party member's command, and `actor` is them |
| `~ one command each` | Every able member of the party gives one command a round; the round goes on when each has (or the lead says `Hold`) |
| `~ at opponent here` | One Link per opponent still standing, `{target}` in its label |
| `wound target 3 ~ as ion` | Damage with a kind |
| `~ resistance kinetic`, `~ weakness ion`, `~ immunity cold` | Half, double, none, of damage of that type; with `when`, only while it holds; a list for several |
| `~ cooldown 3 rounds` | An act or threat that, once used, waits that many rounds; `x.cooling(act)` |
| `pattern … ~ while …` | Pattern phases: the pattern in play is the first whose `while` holds; `on pattern unbound begins` when one takes over |
| `pattern … ~ by weight` | The next move is the heaviest whose `when` holds and is not cooling |
| `unleash klaxon` | A threat from the world, outside any round (the vault's alarm) |
| `lead ivo` | The lead passes to someone else: the pov changes |
| `heal target 4`, `revive target` | `hp` back, up to its start; up again from down |
| `landed` | The outcome once called `hit` |
)))
kind: game
tags: science fantasy ~ party ~ heist ~ boss fight
ages: 10..
mode: solo
pov: ress
start: hangar

character ress: "Ress" ~ like vanguard ~ pronouns he ~ selectable
character ivo: "Ivo" ~ like arcanist ~ pronouns he ~ selectable
character tam: "Tam" ~ like medic ~ pronouns he ~ selectable
character quill: "Quill" ~ like scout ~ pronouns he ~ selectable

place hangar: "the ice hangar"
place gallery: "the long gallery"
place vents: "the coolant vents"
place vault: "the chart vault"
place lift: "the freight lift"
way hangar_door: hangar - gallery
way grille: gallery - vents ~ open when quill.knows.vent_route
way vault_door: gallery - vault ~ open when vault_door_open
way crawl: vents - vault
way lift_gate: vault - lift ~ one way

state vault_door_open: no

item meridian_key: "the Meridian Key, a disc of black glass full of moving stars" ~ in vault ~ evidence
fact vent_route: "Quill reads the coolant plans: the vents run to the back of the vault." ~ clue

(((
Kinds of harm. A tag on an archetype counts for everything like it.
)))
archetype sentry ~ resistance kinetic ~ weakness ion ~ immunity cold
npc sentry_a: "Sentry A" ~ like sentry ~ in hangar
npc sentry_b: "Sentry B" ~ like sentry ~ in hangar
npc orrel: "Prefect Orrel" ~ pronouns she ~ in lift

(((
The vault's alarm: a threat the world makes, once, when the Key leaves its
pillar. Not an opponent's, and not in a round.
)))
threat klaxon: at pov.all ~ answered by cover
~ then wound target 1 ~ as sound

:: vanguard [archetype]
(((
The first of the four classes. Each act is one command; the lead's own is
a command too. `hp` runs out: down, not dead, until revived.
)))
--
stat hp: 14
act strike: cost 0 ~ "a hardlight blade" ~ at opponent here ~ then wound target 3 ~ as kinetic
act shield_wall: cost 0 ~ "a wall of hardlight before the party" ~ cooldown 3 rounds ~ then cover pov.all
act taunt: cost 0 ~ "draws the next blow to himself" ~ then block for pov.all

:: arcanist [archetype]
--
stat hp: 8
act ion_bolt: cost 0 ~ "a bolt of blue lightning" ~ at opponent here ~ then wound target 3 ~ as ion
act frostfall: cost 0 ~ "cold that falls like a curtain" ~ cooldown 2 rounds ~ then wound all(opponent, in: here) 2 ~ as cold
act unseal: cost 0 ~ "talks an Auric lock open" ~ when here.is(gallery) ~ then set vault_door_open: yes

:: medic [archetype]
--
stat hp: 9
act mend: cost 0 ~ "a field graft" ~ at character here ~ when not target.down ~ then heal target 4
act revive: cost 0 ~ "a stimulant, a slap, a prayer" ~ at character here ~ when target.down ~ cooldown 3 rounds ~ then revive target
act screen: cost 0 ~ "a smoke screen" ~ then prevent all(opponent, in: here)

:: scout [archetype]
--
stat hp: 10
act snipe: cost 0 ~ "one round, well placed" ~ at opponent here ~ then wound target 4 ~ as kinetic
act deadeye: cost 0 ~ "the shot you only get once" ~ at opponent here ~ cooldown 4 rounds ~ then wound target 9 ~ as kinetic
act read_plans: cost 0 ~ "reads the relay's plans off a panel" ~ when here.is(gallery) ~ then learn vent_route

:: sentry [archetype]
(((
Hangar sentries: two of them, the same machine.
)))
--
stat hp: 6
pattern sweep: scan, burst ~ repeat ~ one per round
threat scan ~ then set self.locked: yes
threat burst: at one(character, in: here, where: not it.down) ~ answered by cover, block ~ when self.locked
~ then wound target 3

:: orrel_frame [npc]
(((
Prefect Orrel, in the Lamplighter frame: a walking furnace of brass and
hardlight. Armoured, the frame shrugs off kinetic fire; broken, it
doesn't, and Orrel stops following the drill.
)))
--
stat hp: 30
state armoured: yes
~ resistance kinetic when self.armoured
~ weakness ion when not self.armoured
~ immunity cold when self.armoured

pattern drill: lance, sweep_beam, lance, brace ~ repeat ~ one per round ~ while orrel.hp > 15
pattern unbound: overload, call_sentries, lance, sweep_beam ~ by weight ~ one per round ~ while orrel.hp <= 15

threat lance: at one(character, in: here, where: not it.down) ~ answered by cover, block ~ weight 2
~ then wound target 4 ~ as fire
threat sweep_beam: at pov.all ~ answered by cover, prevent ~ weight 3
~ then wound target 2 ~ as fire
threat brace ~ then heal self 3
threat overload: at pov.all ~ answered by prevent ~ weight 6 ~ cooldown 3 rounds
~ then wound target 5 ~ as fire
threat call_sentries ~ weight 4 ~ once ~ when count(sentry, in: here, where: not it.down) == 0
~ then move sentry_a to here ~ then move sentry_b to here
~ then heal sentry_a 6 ~ then heal sentry_b 6

on pattern unbound begins
~ then set orrel.armoured: no
~ then say orrel "Enough. Enough drill."

:: hangar
(((
The sentries: a first, small encounter with two opponents.
)))
encounter sentry_a, sentry_b
~ as fight
~ round by round
~ one command each
~ acts last
~ until count(sentry, in: here, where: not it.down) == 0 or pov.all.down
--
The shuttle sets down on the ice inside the relay’s mouth, and the four of you are out before the ramp has finished falling. Two Auric sentries turn their lamps on you: drones like hanging lanterns, each with a gun where the flame should be.
> [[Fight->hangar:round]] ~ id fight_sentries

:: hangar:round [round]
hint: "Drones are built to stop bullets. Ivo’s lightning goes straight through them."
--
[if count(sentry, in: here, where: it.locked) > 0]
A lamp narrows to a red point on one of you.

[end]
> ~ cost 0
> [[Ress: strike {target}->hangar:after]] ~ strike ~ by ress
> [[Ress: shield wall->hangar:after]] ~ shield_wall ~ by ress ~ when not ress.cooling(shield_wall)
> [[Ivo: ion bolt at {target}->hangar:after]] ~ ion_bolt ~ by ivo
> [[Ivo: frostfall->hangar:after]] ~ frostfall ~ by ivo ~ when not ivo.cooling(frostfall)
> [[Tam: mend {target}->hangar:after]] ~ mend ~ by tam
> [[Tam: smoke screen->hangar:after]] ~ screen ~ by tam
> [[Quill: snipe {target}->hangar:after]] ~ snipe ~ by quill
> [[Hold->hangar:after]] ~ id hold ~ then end round

:: hangar:after [resolve]
--
[if threat.name == burst and threat.outcome == landed]
The burst catches {threat.target}.

[if threat.outcome == cover]
The hardlight wall takes it.

[if count(sentry, in: here, where: not it.down) == 0]
The second lamp gutters and goes out. The hangar is quiet but for the wind.

[end]
> [[Go on->hangar:round]] ~ cost 0 ~ when not encounter.over
> [[Into the relay->gallery]] ~ cost 0 ~ when encounter.over and not pov.all.down
> [[…->captured]] ~ cost 0 ~ when pov.all.down

:: gallery
--
A gallery a hundred yards long, lit by lamps in cages. At the far end, the vault door: a disc of brass with no handle, only an Auric seal that hums.
> [[Ivo: work the seal->gallery]] ~ unseal ~ by ivo ~ when not vault_door_open
> [[Quill: read the relay’s plans->gallery]] ~ read_plans ~ by quill ~ when not quill.knows.vent_route
> [[Give the lead to {target}->gallery]] ~ at character here ~ when target != pov ~ then lead target
> [[Through the vault door->vault]] ~ when vault_door_open
> [[Into the vents->vents]] ~ when quill.knows.vent_route

:: vents
--
A crawl through tubes furred with frost. Your breath freezes on the metal.
> [[Drop into the vault->vault]]

:: vault
--
The chart vault: a dome of black glass, and in the middle of it, on a pillar of light, the Meridian Key.
> [[Take the Key->vault:take]] ~ when meridian_key.in(vault)
> [[To the freight lift->lift]] ~ when me.holds(meridian_key)

:: vault:take [act]
gain meridian_key
unleash klaxon
--
The light goes out. Then every light in the relay comes on red, and a voice you will hear in your sleep says the same word in four languages.

The freight lift is the only way up. Something very large is standing in it.


:: lift
encounter orrel
~ as fight
~ round by round
~ one command each
~ acts last
~ until orrel.hp == 0 or pov.all.down
--
Prefect Orrel fills the lift: nine feet of brass frame with a woman’s face in the furnace-window of its chest, calm as a clerk.

“Four Lanterns,” she says. “And the Key. Put it on the floor and I’ll make it quick.”
> [[Fight->lift:round]] ~ id fight_orrel

:: lift:round [round]
let next: orrel.pattern.next
hint: "The frame turns bullets while it’s whole. Break it with lightning, then shoot it." ~ when orrel.armoured
hint: "Overload hits all of you, hard. Tam’s smoke stops it, if he’s ready." ~ when next == overload
--
[if next == lance]
The frame lowers a lance of white fire at one of you.

[if next == sweep_beam]
The furnace-window brightens. Something is about to sweep the whole lift.

[if next == overload]
Every vent on the frame opens at once. The air shakes.

[if next == call_sentries]
Orrel speaks into her collar.

[if orrel.armoured; append]
Her armour gleams, unscratched.

[end]
> ~ cost 0
> [[Ress: strike {target}->lift:after]] ~ strike ~ by ress
> [[Ress: shield wall->lift:after]] ~ shield_wall ~ by ress ~ when not ress.cooling(shield_wall)
> [[Ress: taunt->lift:after]] ~ taunt ~ by ress
> [[Ivo: ion bolt at {target}->lift:after]] ~ ion_bolt ~ by ivo
> [[Ivo: frostfall->lift:after]] ~ frostfall ~ by ivo ~ when not ivo.cooling(frostfall)
> [[Tam: mend {target}->lift:after]] ~ mend ~ by tam
> [[Tam: revive {target}->lift:after]] ~ revive ~ by tam ~ when not tam.cooling(revive)
> [[Tam: smoke screen->lift:after]] ~ screen ~ by tam
> [[Quill: snipe {target}->lift:after]] ~ snipe ~ by quill
> [[Quill: deadeye on {target}->lift:after]] ~ deadeye ~ by quill ~ when not quill.cooling(deadeye)
> [[Hold->lift:after]] ~ id hold_lift ~ then end round

:: lift:after [resolve]
--
[if threat.name == lance and threat.outcome == landed]
The lance takes {threat.target} full in the chest.

[if threat.name == overload and threat.outcome == prevent]
Tam’s smoke rolls through the lift, and the overload vents into nothing.

[if threat.name == overload and threat.outcome == landed]
The overload throws all four of you against the lift wall.

[if threat.outcome == cover]
The hardlight wall holds.

[if threat.outcome == block]
Ress steps into it.

[if orrel.hp == 0]
The frame kneels, very slowly, like a camel. The furnace goes out.

[end]
> [[Go on->lift:round]] ~ cost 0 ~ when not encounter.over
> [[Up->extraction]] ~ cost 0 ~ when encounter.over and not pov.all.down
> [[…->captured]] ~ cost 0 ~ when pov.all.down

:: extraction [finale]
--
The lift rises into the dark. At the top there is wind, and stars, and the shuttle with its ramp already down.

[if count(character, where: it.down) == 0]
All four of you walk up the ramp. Quill is laughing.

[else]
You carry {plural(count(character, where: it.down), "one of your own", "two of your own")} up the ramp between you.

[end]
In Ress’s pocket, the Meridian Key turns its slow stars.

:: captured [finale]
--
The Dominion is polite to its prisoners. That is the most frightening thing about it.

:: ion_breaks_a_drone [test]
start: hangar
do: "Fight"
do: "Ivo: ion bolt at Sentry A"
expect: sentry_a.hp == 0
(((
A weakness to ion: 3, doubled, of 6.
)))

:: bullets_glance_off_the_frame [test]
start: lift
do: "Fight"
do: "Quill: snipe Orrel"
expect: orrel.hp == 28
(((
A resistance to kinetic while armoured: 4, halved.
)))

:: each_ally_one_command [test]
start: hangar
do: "Fight"
do: "Ivo: ion bolt at Sentry A"
expect no link: "Ivo: frostfall"
expect link: "Quill: snipe Sentry B"

:: a_cooldown_waits [test]
start: lift
do: "Fight"
do: "Quill: deadeye on Orrel"
do: "Hold"
do: "Go on"
expect: quill.cooling(deadeye)
expect no link: "Quill: deadeye on Orrel"

:: the_frame_breaks_at_half [test]
start: lift
do: "Fight"
given: set orrel.hp: 15
do: "Hold"
expect: not orrel.armoured
do: "Go on"
expect: orrel.pattern.next in [overload, call_sentries, lance, sweep_beam]

:: the_lead_changes_hands [test]
start: gallery
do: "Give the lead to Ivo"
expect: pov == ivo

:: the_alarm_rings_out_of_turn [test]
start: vault
do: "Take the Key"
expect: ress.hp == 13 and quill.hp == 9
